[81.624315, "o", "\u001b[?25l\r\n\r\n \u001b[1m←\u001b[m open sidebar · Interactive · Manual Approval · \u001b[1m/\u001b[m commands · \u001b[1m?\u001b[m help · \u001b[1mtab\u001b[m next tab\u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[81.657722, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[3;109H\u001b[1K\r\n \u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[1msaia_generate_spl \u001b[m(MC… {\"results\":[{\"response\":[\"| @spl2 from index:demo_soc\\n| where sourcetype=\\... 44s\u001b[B\u001b[1K\r\n \u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[1mCreate \u001b[moptimized_login_failure_rate.spl2 \u001b[32m+7\u001b[m                                                          \r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n \u001b[34m●\u001b[m I saved the rewrite as \u001b[37m optimized_login_failure_rate.spl2 \u001b[m. I haven't run it yet. I dropped the returned\r\n   leading \u001b[37m |  \u001b[m so the file matches the original's format. Add the \u001b[37m |  \u001b[m prefix when running it.\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   \u001b[1mWhat changed\u001b[m                                                                \r\n\r\n   • \u001b[1;37m join \u001b[39m removed:\u001b[m a single \u001b[37m stats \u001b[m computes \u001b[37m attempts \u001b[m and \u001b[37m failures \u001b[m (\u001b[37m sum(is_failure) \u001b[m) in one pass.   \r\n     The original scanned the data twice and joined the results, so this should roughly halve the scan.  \r\n   • \u001b[1;37m is_failure \u001b[39m is now used:\u001b[m the original computed it and never used it.\r\n   •"]
[81.657736, "o", " \u001b[1mFewer steps:\u001b[m the extra \u001b[37m eval \u001b[m that renamed the \u001b[37m L. \u001b[m/\u001b[37m R. \u001b[m fields is gone. The output fields and the\r\n     \u001b[37m failure_rate \u001b[m calculation are unchanged.                                           \u001b[14C     \r\n   • \u001b[1;37m index=* \u001b[39m became \u001b[37m from index:demo_soc \u001b[39m:\u001b[m this is the main reason it should run faster, since it scans\r\n     one index instead of all of them.                                                             \r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   \u001b[1mCaveat:\u001b[m SAIA added \u001b[37m index:demo_soc \u001b[m on its own, and I haven't checked that \u001b[37m portal:auth \u001b[m lives only\u001b[7C┃\r\r\n   there. If it is also in other indexes, the results will differ from the baseline. The wider \u001b[37m index=* \u001b[m     ┃\r\r\n   scan is a large part of the baseline cost.\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   I'd run it and compare it to the baseline (91.56 s, 1,421,600 events, 4 results). If the rows differ,\r\n   \u001b[37m index=* \u001b[m or an explicit index list is needed. Want me to run it?\u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[82.657736, "o", "\u001b[?25lR\r\n\r\n Interactive · Manual Approval · \u001b[1m@\u001b[m files/sessions · \u001b[1m#\u001b[m issues                        \u001b[30;4H\u001b[?25h"]
