[105.417234, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[3;4H\u001b[90m│\u001b[m Runtime      \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 91.56 s   \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 2.47 s (about 37× faster) \u001b[90m│\r\n\u001b[3C├──────────────┼───────────┼───────────────────────────┤\r\n\u001b[3C│\u001b[m Event count  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 1,421,600 \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 1,421,600                 \u001b[90m│\u001b[m                                             \r\n   \u001b[90m├──────────────┼───────────┼───────────────────────────┤\u001b[m         \r\n   \u001b[90m│\u001b[m Result count \u001b[90m│\u001b[m 4\u001b[7;31H\u001b[90m│\u001b[m 4\u001b[7;59H\u001b[90m│\r\n\u001b[C\u001b[m  \u001b[90m└──────────────┴───────────┴───────────────────────────┘\u001b[m                                                 \u001b[B\u001b[1K\r\n   \u001b[1mJob messages and warnings:\u001b[m none appeared in \u001b[37m jobs status \u001b[m or \u001b[37m jo"]
[105.417247, "o", "bs show \u001b[m. I didn't check Job Inspector or\r\n   \u001b[37m search.log \u001b[m.                                \r\n\r\n   \u001b[1mOutput rows:\u001b[m all four rows match the baseline on \u001b[37m service \u001b[m, \u001b[37m version \u001b[m, \u001b[37m attempts \u001b[m, \u001b[37m failures \u001b[m and\r\n   \u001b[37m failure_rate \u001b[m, with the same 30.8% for \u001b[37m mobile-login v4.12.0 \u001b[m and 2.0% for the other three. The three   \r\n   2.0% rows came back in a different order (the baseline listed mobile-login v4.11.3 above sso-bridge).    \r\n   They tie on \u001b[37m failure_rate \u001b[m, so the sort doesn't fix their order.                                         \r\n\r\n   \u001b[1mParity:\u001b[m the row contents are identical in this run. I'm not claiming general equivalence for two reasons:\r\n\r\n   • \u001b[1mIndex scope:\u001b[m the rewrite reads only \u001b[37m demo_soc \u001b[m instead of \u001b[37m index=* \u001b[m. The matching event counts suggest\r\n     all the \u001b[37m portal:auth \u001b[m data sits in that index for this time range, but a different range or newly added\r\n     indexes could differ. "]
[105.417261, "o", "                              \r\n   • \u001b[1mTie ordering:\u001b[m if row order matters, add a secondary sort key such as \u001b[37m service, version \u001b[m.\u001b[16C┃\r\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   The speedup comes from one scan instead of two, no \u001b[37m join \u001b[m, and a single-index scan. With the event counts\r\n   unchanged, I can't tell how much each of the three contributed.\u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
